Structure of the Project 

This project is designed for children, parents, and educators who are seeking an accessible and effective way to support a child’s development.

The idea began during one of Apple’s VisionOS development events, where they demonstrated an educational app showing the layers of the Earth. I already knew about the layers themselves, but seeing them presented in that format sparked something in me. The idea of expanding that concept into a broader educational app—one that could even be adapted for VisionOS or other VR headsets—stuck with me. Of course, considering age restrictions for VR use, only certain parts of the app would be appropriate for VR, but the potential still inspired me. The thought stayed with me and never left. Eventually, I decided to pursue it—thinking not only of my own child, but of children around the world, and those who are yet to come.

Montessori is a well-known educational approach used in many countries, but it has one major challenge: it can be expensive, and many families simply cannot afford it. My goal is to make high-quality, Montessori-inspired learning tools as affordable and accessible as possible, so that anyone—parents, teachers, or anyone wishing to share knowledge—can use them at any time.

This will be a long journey, but one worth taking. With my experience as a parent, my background in education, and my growing knowledge of technology, I believe this is the right path and the right moment to take this risk.

